      "type": "buttonedge",
      "id": "bufferMemory_0-bufferMemory_0-output-bufferMemory-BufferMemory|BaseChatMemory|BaseMemory-conversationChain_0-conversationChain_0-input-memory-BaseMemory"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "# LiteLLM Quick Start Template\n\nThis chatflow demonstrates the recommended way to integrate Flowise with LiteLLM.\n\n## Key Configuration\n\n1. **ChatOpenAI Node**:\n   - BasePath: `http://litellm:4000` (routes to LiteLLM proxy)\n   - Model: `gpt-3.5-turbo` (but works with any LiteLLM model)\n   - Credential: Select your \"LiteLLM Proxy\" credential\n\n2. **Available Models**:\n   - OpenAI: gpt-4, gpt-4-turbo, gpt-3.5-turbo\n   - Anthropic: claude-3-opus, claude-3-sonnet, claude-3-haiku\n   - Local: llama3:8b, codegemma (via Ollama)\n\n## Before Using\n\n1. Create credential in Flowise:\n   - Go to Credentials → Add New\n   - Type: OpenAI API\n   - Name: LiteLLM Proxy\n   - API Key: Your LITELLM_MASTER_KEY\n\n2. Verify LiteLLM is running:\n   ```bash\n   curl http://localhost:4000/health\n   ```\n\n3. After import:\n   - Select your credential in the ChatOpenAI node\n   - Choose your preferred model\n   - Test the chatflow\n\n## Testing\n\nTry these example prompts:\n- \"What model are you using?\"\n- \"Can you explain what LiteLLM is?\"\n- \"Tell me a joke\"\n\n## Switching Models\n\nTo use a different model:\n1. Click on the ChatOpenAI node\n2. Change the Model Name field\n3. Models from different providers work the same way!\n\n## More Information\n\nSee `docs/flowise-litellm-setup.md` for complete setup guide."
}
